/> Ran?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T05:03:54-07:00","id":1204155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1204005-our-lady-of-the-waters?p=1204122#post1204122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tiamat?<br /> <br /> Ran?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who/what\u2019s Ran?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T05:22:48-07:00","id":1204160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1204005-our-lady-of-the-waters?p=1204155#post1204155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who/what\u2019s Ran?</div> </div> </div> </div>A norse goddess of the sea, wife of Aegir. It's at one of their parties that Loki roasts the whole pantheon to the point the Aesir have enough with him. Ran has a somewhat sinister reputation, with some sources associating her with death at sea, shipwrecks and a penchant for drowning people.<br /> <br /> I don't think the Lady is meant to be a reference to either her or Tiamat, tough: both are oceanic beings while the Lady is clearly said to belong to rivers and lakes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T14:41:55-07:00","id":1205367,"title":"","content":"I'd kind of gotten the feeling she at least <i>can</i> represent the idea of the river/lake monster itself, or at least some of the more common legends (the Loch Ness Monster and similar). Don't know if it's what the writer was going for, but the text <i>does</i> call out rivers and lakes in a lot of places where those kinds of stories are popular-ish, so there's at least some support in there for it. And while this bit is pretty indirect and vague to base a guess off of, her entry does imply a link between her and the Old Man of the Mountains if I'm reading it right (calling him &quot;her favorite brother&quot;), and both Bigfoot-like figures and lake monsters are some of the more popular modern-ish legends (and from there among the first things that come to mind when someone mentions words like &quot;cryptozoology&quot;).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, this could just be the last lingering dregs of my inner middle-school-aged &quot;aspiring cryptozoologist/paranormal investigator&quot; peeking out, so take this post with a grain of salt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 04-10-2018, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T00:27:22-07:00","id":1205484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sconce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1204005-our-lady-of-the-waters?p=1205367#post1205367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd kind of gotten the feeling she at least <i>can</i> represent the idea of the river/lake monster itself, or at least some of the more common legends (the Loch Ness Monster and similar). Don't know if it's what the writer was going for, but the text <i>does</i> call out rivers and lakes in a lot of places where those kinds of stories are popular-ish, so there's at least some support in there for it. And while this bit is pretty indirect and vague to base a guess off of, her entry does imply a link between her and the Old Man of the Mountains if I'm reading it right (calling him &quot;her favorite brother&quot;), and both Bigfoot-like figures and lake monsters are some of the more popular modern-ish legends (and from there among the first things that come to mind when someone mentions words like &quot;cryptozoology&quot;).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, this could just be the last lingering dregs of my inner middle-school-aged &quot;aspiring cryptozoologist/paranormal investigator&quot; peeking out, so take this post with a grain of salt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No that makes sense to me actually, it is true when you think cryptids bigfoot and nessie are the first to come to mind. I'll probably roll with that. Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T10:00:34-07:00","id":1206498,"title":"","content":"I was, in fact, using the myths and legends of lake/river monsters as my inspiration here, specifically Mokele-mbembe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Wyrd Sister<br /> Freelance Penmonkey For Hire<br /> Moloch's PR Chick</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3896-nagaina","name":"Nagaina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T12:55:53-07:00","id":1206597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nagaina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1204005-our-lady-of-the-waters?p=1206498#post1206498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was, in fact, using the myths and legends of lake/river monsters as my inspiration here, specifically Mokele-mbembe.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you so much for confirming!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}